.TH CTOOLS 1 "2026-10-23" "ctools" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ctools \- navigate, search, and copy the sessions of LLM agents
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ctools
.I command
.RI [ args ...]
.br
.B ctools
.RB [ \-h | \-\-help | \-\-version ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ctools
is the front door to the ctools commands. Each
.I command
runs the same program as its short name, with the same options:
.B ctools grep
is
.BR cgrep ,
.B ctools copy
is
.BR ccopy ,
and so on. Everything after the command is passed through unchanged, and
help and error messages name the command as you typed it.
.PP
With no command,
.BR \-h ,
.BR \-\-help ,
or
.BR help ,
.B ctools
prints the list of commands below.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS Query
.TP
.BR dir " (" cdir )
List agents and sessions.
.TP
.BR grep " (" cgrep )
Search session content.
.TP
.BR cat " (" ccat )
Print a session.
.TP
.BR du " (" cdu )
Context usage per session.
.SS Transform
.TP
.BR copy " (" ccopy )
Copy a session to another agent.
.TP
.BR extract " (" cextract )
Extract concepts from a session.
.TP
.BR connect " (" cconnect )
Pipe concepts between sessions.
.TP
.BR rm " (" crm )
Cut sections out of a session.
.TP
.BR recover " (" crecover )
Restore from a backup.
.SS Long-running
.TP
.BR web " (" ctools-web )
Run the web dashboard.
.TP
.BR mcp " (" ctools-mcp )
Run the MCP server.
.PP
Run
.B ctools
.I command
.B \-\-help
for a command's options.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print the list of commands and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print version information and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
ctools dir                              # every known agent
ctools grep -i "deploy" claude-code     # search one agent
ctools cat --text opencode/ses_abc      # read a session
ctools copy opencode/ses_abc codex      # copy it into another agent
ctools copy opencode/ses_abc ssh://me@box/   # into opencode on another host
.fi
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Help or version printed; otherwise the command's own exit status.
.TP
.B 2
Unknown command.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cdir (1),
.BR cgrep (1),
.BR ccat (1),
.BR cdu (1),
.BR ccopy (1),
.BR cextract (1)
.SH AUTHORS
ctools project.
